    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A4.SS2",
    "original_text": "Attributed implementation/Jensen component of Algorithm D.2 and Lemma D.4, not full D.4. Retain the normalized C2 Hessian bounds, kappa>=1, 0<eta<=c<1 and eps>0. Suppose q:E->E and N:E->Nat satisfy the actual stopped gradient interpreter equation run(grad V,eta,eps,y,N(y)+1,y)=some(q(y),N(y)+1) for every y. For any probability measure mu on an arbitrary measurable space and measurable realized center Y with integrable ||grad V(Y)||^2, the same count N(Y)+1 is integrable and its expectation is at most C_c[1+log(1+sqrt(E_mu||grad V(Y)||^2)/eps)], where C_c=2+(1+log((1-c)^(-1)))/(-log c). Successful interpreter outputs and counts are independent of sufficient fuel; this identifies the supplied implementation with the already compiled expected-work witness before pulling its bound back along Y. No count measurability or integrability is assumed. The actual run-wide moment D.7 and aggregation D.8 are separate.",
    "text_sha256": "bb22bb45aabd5f7532e959fef7189b9d16110654085bc60e1b4e72850fea5b8d"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.RealizedProximalWork.realized_proximal_expected_work",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/RealizedProximalWork.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α] (μ : Measure α) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ≥0} (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (κ : ℝ)⁻¹ * ‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta c eps : ℝ} (heta : 0 < eta) (hec : eta ≤ c) (hc : c < 1) (heps : 0 < eps)\n    (q : E → E) (N : E → ℕ)\n    (hrun : ∀ y, run (gradient V) eta eps y\n      (N y + 1) y = some (q y, N y + 1))\n    (Y : α → E) (hY : Measurable Y)\n    (hmoment : Integrable (fun ω => ‖gradient V (Y ω)‖^2) μ) :\n    Integrable (fun ω => (N (Y ω) : ℝ) + 1) μ ∧\n      (∫ ω, (N (Y ω) : ℝ) + 1 ∂μ) ≤\n        (2 + (1 + Real.log ((1-c)⁻¹)) / (-Real.log c)) *\n          (1 + Real.log (1 + Real.sqrt (∫ ω, ‖gradient V (Y ω)‖^2 ∂μ) / eps))",
    "statement_sha256": "0bbdd735512c022206260f1181bc3fe3361ccadca453f84805af5b435f19e622",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "The finite interpreter run(g,eta,eps,y,fuel,x) returns none at zero fuel; at positive fuel it evaluates g(x), sets next=y-eta*g(x), and returns some(x,1) if ||next-x||<=(1-eta)*eps. Otherwise it recurses at next with one less fuel and adds one to a successful returned query count. All arithmetic is exact real arithmetic.",
      "Integrable is Bochner integrability with respect to the specified measure. A probability measure has total mass one. gradient is the real inner-product gradient, and fderiv is the real Frechet derivative. N takes values in natural numbers; (N y : real)+1 counts all gradient tests including the final successful test."
    ]
  },
  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space equipped with its Borel measurable structure. Let (A,mu) be any measurable probability space. Let V:E->R be C^2 and kappa be a nonnegative real with 1<=kappa, and assume that for every x,v in E,\n  kappa^(-1)||v||^2 <= D^2 V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2.\nLet eta,c,epsilon be real numbers with 0<eta<=c<1 and epsilon>0. Fix arbitrary functions q:E->E and N:E->N such that for every y in E,\n  run(grad V,eta,epsilon,y,N(y)+1,y)=some(q(y),N(y)+1).\nHere the finite interpreter run(g,eta,epsilon,y,fuel,x) returns none at zero fuel. With positive fuel it evaluates g(x) and sets next=y-eta g(x). It returns (x,1) when ||next-x||<=(1-eta)epsilon; otherwise it recurses from next with fuel decreased by one and adds one to a successful returned query count. Arithmetic is exact real arithmetic. Consequently N(y)+1 is the reported number of gradient tests, including the final successful test, for this successful run initialized at y.\nFor every measurable Y:A->E such that omega -> ||grad V(Y(omega))||^2 is integrable with respect to mu, the real-valued test count omega -> N(Y(omega))+1 is integrable with respect to mu, and\n  integral_A (N(Y(omega))+1) dmu(omega)\n    <= [2+(1+log((1-c)^(-1)))/(-log c)]\n       [1+log(1+sqrt(integral_A ||grad V(Y(omega))||^2 dmu(omega))/epsilon)].\nNatural counts in this formula are cast to the reals. Integrability is Bochner integrability. The logarithm is the real logarithm and the square root is the real square root. The conclusions concern the integrability and expected count of the stipulated successful exact-arithmetic interpreter; no existence of q or N, explicit pointwise complexity bound, output-error guarantee, sampling-kernel property, or convergence statement is asserted by this theorem.",
    "text_sha256": "89df144815055d76475649ebacff242b57032440ebb2c6cb613be862668165e2",
    "decoder": "anonymous_decoder_20261005",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "d59e9133f36aa9fff20084ff141539fb55ef4264af318d0fa9e89da604de268b",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "c0e81559f50c4ea5ba808096b02d1c1b668246457416d139a252ab8fb1faa247",
    "source_text_visible": false,
